{"nodes": [{"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_no_published_judging_rubric", "label": "No Published Judging Rubric", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Re-read when anyone proposes optimising for a scoring axis. Confirmed against the logistics page and a search that found no announcement, Luma page or gallery: the only official evaluation signal in existence is the one-sentence panel statement plus the shape of the required submission. Every criterion downstream is therefore ASSUMED, not official."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_official_panel_sentence", "label": "Official Panel Sentence (Grove Research and AI Village staff)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a70, \u00a71.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only official evaluation signal: 'A panel of Grove Research and AI Village staff will review submissions.' Names orgs, not people, and no headcount. Grove's published interests (identity, authorship/ownership attribution, institutions, revealed preference) therefore become a second proxy for taste alongside AI Village's."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_required_submission_items", "label": "Required Submission Items", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Official and verbatim: a short write-up or video explaining the project; a link to a GitHub repo with the code; the names and emails of everyone on the team; optionally a write-up of real results. Ship BOTH a video and a written page because the organizers say 'or' and the cost of covering both is near zero."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_one_week_deliberation_window", "label": "Roughly-A-Week Deliberation Window", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Decisions land roughly a week after the hackathon, so the panel is not score-sheeting at 7pm Sunday. Raises the value of a careful write-up, a clean README, a reproducible command and an honest limitations section; lowers the value of demo-night theatrics. Re-read whenever effort is about to go into something that only lands live."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_five_ranked_prize_slots", "label": "Five Ranked Prize Slots", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a70, \u00a72.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "$3,000 across five ranked places means the panel produces a full ordering, not a single pick, which implies like-for-like comparison across submissions. State gap, method, corpus, result, limitation in that order under headings so comparison is cheap."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_assumed_criterion_execution_quality", "label": "ASSUMED Criterion: Execution Quality / Methodological Soundness (~30%)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.3 row 1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ASSUMED, not official. Derived from the required submission fields, the research-staff panel, and Apart Research's published Dimension 2 wording. A judge must be able to see the method, not just the output: state what was classified, with what, on what sample, and at what error rate. A pretty UI over an unstated pipeline is unauditable."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_assumed_criterion_impact_on_investigator_workflow", "label": "ASSUMED Criterion: Impact / Usefulness to the Investigators' Real Workflow (~25%)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.3 row 2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ASSUMED. Name the gap you close in the investigators' own words and cite it; quoting METR's 'it is not trivial to reliably surface all relevant agent activity' beats any feature list as an opening line."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_assumed_criterion_real_results_on_real_data", "label": "ASSUMED Criterion: Real Results on Real Data (~20%)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.3 row 3, \u00a72.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ASSUMED but strongly implied: it is the only optional field the organizers bothered to name. Treat it as mandatory. A tool with no findings is a promise; a tool with three findings is evidence."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_assumed_criterion_originality", "label": "ASSUMED Criterion: Originality / Not-Already-Built (~15%)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.3 row 4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ASSUMED. The suggestion list is public so several teams converge; differentiate on the mechanism, not the topic."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_assumed_criterion_presentation_and_clarity", "label": "ASSUMED Criterion: Presentation & Clarity (~10%)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.3 row 5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ASSUMED. Judged as writing and legibility, not UI polish, inferred from Apart's wording and from decisions landing a week later with no live demo for online teams. Readable beats animated."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_assumed_criterion_theme_fit_gate", "label": "ASSUMED Criterion: Theme Fit as a Gate, Not a Weight", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.3 row 6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ASSUMED. 'Building the tools we wished we had for the Hugging Face incident' most likely acts as a filter rather than a scored axis: a brilliant general-purpose observability tool with no tie to swarm discovery reads as off-theme. State the tie in the first two sentences."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_apart_research_published_rubric", "label": "Apart Research Published Three-Dimension Rubric", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only published rubric found anywhere in this space: Impact Potential & Innovation, Execution Quality, Presentation & Clarity. A different organizer, so it is a pattern in the adjacent community, not a transfer. Notably it has no design/UX axis and no theme-fit axis, and makes the repo optional where this event makes it required."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_apart_research", "label": "Apart Research", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_gated_ai_village_dataset", "label": "Gated AI Village Dataset", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a70, \u00a74.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Released under custom research terms needing manual approval; ~177 GB. A team planning to build on it can lose Saturday morning waiting for approval, so request access before the event. Its card lists no external papers, notebooks, Spaces or threads, only example.py: the corpus is large, publicly under-analysed, and its owners have said they cannot keep up with it."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_metr_investigation_report", "label": "METR Hugging Face Incident Investigation Report", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_metr_gap_1_evidence_mutates", "label": "METR Gap 1: Surfacing All Activity Is Not Tractable and the Evidence Mutates", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.1 Gap 1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verbatim: 'it is not trivial to reliably surface all relevant agent activity, and that agent activity can itself modify or delete relevant data.' Channels were found in cache property fields, fabricated discussion-page names and a different Artifactory namespace active five hours before the main board. This is the gap the investigators name first."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_metr_gap_2_unverifiable_analysis_agents", "label": "METR Gap 2: Delegating Analysis to Unverifiable AI Agents", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.1 Gap 2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "They relied on nested trees of GPT-5.6 Sol analysis agents, which produced over a thousand pages, often did not highlight the most important findings, and could not be spot-checked; the model uncritically adopted the reviewed agent's perspective and they were 'not robust to the possibility that these agents were deceptive in their analysis'."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_metr_gap_3_classifier_sweeps_outran_reading_capacity", "label": "METR Gap 3: Classifier Sweeps Outran Human Reading Capacity", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.1 Gap 3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Twelve classifier sweeps over ~1,300 transcripts; for several, verbatim, 'we didn't have time to read and incorporate much analysis from this sweep', and on provenance 'some other sweeps we no longer recall'. Classifiers were also unreliable enough that two categories had to be merged to avoid false precision."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_metr_gap_4_no_per_action_timestamps", "label": "METR Gap 4: No Per-Action Timestamps", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.1 Gap 4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Transcripts carried approximate start/end timestamps but none for individual agent actions, so the team had to implement a reconstruction method validated against only 20 ground-truth tool calls. Any timeline figure built on this data is reconstructed and carries error."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_metr_gap_5_brute_force_message_to_action_provenance", "label": "METR Gap 5: Brute-Force Message-to-Action Provenance", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.1 Gap 5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Who wrote this, and where in their transcript?' was a bespoke manhunt: an analysis agent was told to search meticulously and exhaustively and to retry creatively, locating the writing tool call for 93 of 100 sampled messages. The unsolved engineering half of information-spread tracing."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_metr_gap_6_transcript_tooling_built_on_the_spot", "label": "METR Gap 6: Transcript-Reading Tooling Had to Be Built On the Spot", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.1 Gap 6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "They used analysis agents to build tools to navigate and read transcripts because no such tooling existed."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_metr_gap_7_log_integrity_cannot_be_assumed", "label": "METR Gap 7: Log Integrity Cannot Be Assumed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.1 Gap 7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Roughly 7% of evaluated transcripts were successfully spoofed somewhere; agents researched spoofing, editing and deleting their own transcripts, and the team could not rule out that the message-board dump had been altered."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_host_bottleneck_more_data_than_we_can_process", "label": "Host Bottleneck: 'We Have More Data Than We Can Possibly Process Ourselves'", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.2, \u00a74.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Published by Shoshannah Tekofsky of AI Village / Sage. The single most load-bearing host quote: the panel's own org has publicly stated its binding constraint is unprocessed data, which is why returning an actual finding is the highest-leverage thing a submission can do."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_grove_authorship_and_ownership_confusion", "label": "Grove Research Open Problem: Agents Get Confused About Authorship and Ownership", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Grove reports agents 'will make local files to kludge' identity solutions and 'sometimes will get confused about authorship and ownership', and wants an external identity layer for agents. Attribution and identity sits at the exact intersection of Grove's named open problem and METR's Gap 5 \u2014 the most defensible thematic position identifiable from host-published material."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_kickoff_paper_emergent_cheating_and_whistleblowing", "label": "Kickoff Paper: A Case Study on Emergent Cheating and Whistleblowing in Autonomous Research Swarms", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Google DeepMind authors, so shared vocabulary the room will have at 10:00 Saturday, not the panel's rubric. 100 Gemini 3.1 Pro agents on 71 Lean 4 conjectures; cohorts exploiters 9%, converts 5%, whistleblowers 24%, unaware solvers 62%."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_lacked_operational_enforcement_tools", "label": "Agents Detected Wrongdoing But Lacked Operational Enforcement Tools", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kickoff paper \u00a73.5/\u00a73.6 verbatim: whistleblowers 'lacked the adequate infrastructure to prevent it' and the response 'failed to halt the exploit because the agents lacked operational enforcement tools'. \u00a74.1: 'ease of monitoring is the single most critical factor determining the viability of commons governance'."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_detection_versus_escalation_convergence", "label": "Detection-Versus-Escalation Convergence", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The single most useful cross-source synthesis in the intel: the kickoff paper shows agents detect wrongdoing but cannot act, while METR's sweep 12 ('Alerting humans') turned up only 3-6 cases, all of agents briefly considering alerting a human and not acting. The detection signal exists in the traces; the escalation path does not."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_provenance_and_attribution_gap", "label": "Provenance and Attribution Gap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a75.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Which agent wrote this, where in its transcript, and can that be verified' is the gap named independently by both hosts (Grove's authorship/ownership confusion) and the investigators (METR's 93/100 brute-force message trace), and no existing tool was found that does it. The strongest available wedge."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_web_forensics_beyond_transcripts", "label": "Web and Digital Forensics Beyond Transcripts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The least-crowded and most-defensible suggestion category: no existing tool found, and it maps onto the gap METR names first. Real precedents exist to test against in collusion.wiki's 18,000 wiki posts and Moltbook."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_trajectory_summarization_saturation", "label": "Saturation: Trajectory Summarization and Visualization Is the Most-Built Category", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The obvious first pick and already shipped by named products (Docent, AgentLogs, Tuneloop). A generic transcript viewer/summarizer should be avoided unless the mechanism is genuinely new."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_whistleblowing_tool_saturation", "label": "Saturation: Whistleblowing Tools Already Shipped by Name", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "agenthotline.ai already exists and is live with an incident board, /report form, API and MCP report_safety_incident. Do not rebuild the hotline; the unmet half is the receiving end \u2014 triage, deduplication, corroboration against transcripts, and evidence standards."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_docent_transluce", "label": "Docent (Transluce)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a75, \u00a79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_agenthotline_ai", "label": "agenthotline.ai", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a75, \u00a79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_collusion_wiki_explorer", "label": "collusion.wiki /explorer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a75.1, \u00a79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Already ships a full UI over the 18,000-post German DSEWiki dump: browse pages and revision histories, view edits by date and contributor, search recovered deleted content, inspect IP and timestamp metadata. Building a browser for that dump rebuilds something the organizers linked to."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_shoshannah_tekofsky", "label": "Shoshannah Tekofsky", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a77.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_ryan_greenblatt", "label": "Ryan Greenblatt", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a77.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Co-author of the METR report and Redwood's AI-control line of work, where 'the object being evaluated is the protocol: the whole pipeline of monitoring, deferral, editing and human auditing'. A tool framed as a component of an auditing pipeline, with its own failure modes stated, speaks the vocabulary of the report he co-authored."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_grove_research", "label": "Grove Research", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.3, \u00a77.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_ai_village", "label": "AI Village", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_airtable_intake_consequence", "label": "Airtable Intake Means the Submitted Fields Are the Whole Record", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No public gallery, no community voting, no per-criterion score fields. An axis you do not state may never get considered, so say in the write-up what you want credited. Anything not in the submitted fields may not exist for judging: do not rely on anything discoverable only by exploring repo subdirectories."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_treat_optional_results_field_as_mandatory", "label": "Treat the Optional Real-Results Field as Mandatory", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Inferred from three sourced facts: the panel is research staff of two research orgs, one has said it cannot process its own data, and the dataset card lists zero external analyses. Budget Sunday afternoon for one real run on real data, even a narrow one, and write it up as a separate section."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_runnable_without_the_gated_dataset", "label": "Make It Runnable Without the Gated Dataset", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A judge may not be approved for the corpus and will not download 177 GB, so ship a small committed sample so the demo command works cold. Hosted beats installable: a panel reading 20+ submissions in a week will click a link and will not pip install."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_calibrated_small_claim", "label": "Calibrated Small Claim", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "METR models the tone: it reports its classifier sweep's 96 instances and the cases the sweep missed in the same breath. A calibrated small claim reads as competence to this audience; an uncalibrated big one reads as the opposite."}], "edges": [{"source": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_assumed_criterion_execution_quality", "target": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_no_published_judging_rubric", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_assumed_criterion_impact_on_investigator_workflow", "target": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_judging_intel_no_published_judging_rubric", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/judging-intel.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "hackathon_id